(5748792, 836819, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives: You have the exposure and focus across the scene here just right and I suspect that wasn''t as straightforward as it might appear. I really like the repeating pattern of the pillars and I particularly like the patterned wall back right of the image. <br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Of course, one of the things that makes the scene remarkable - the emptiness limits the amount of intrinsic interest in this scene and that will be a problem for some.<br/> <br/>Overall: A very well executed capture of an everyday scene.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives: You have the exposure and focus across the scene here just right and I suspect that wasn''t as straightforward as it might appear. I really like the repeating pattern of the pillars and I particularly like the patterned wall back right of the image.  Critical stuff: Of course, one of the things that makes the scene remarkable - the emptiness limits the amount of intrinsic interest in this scene and that will be a problem for some. Overall: A very well executed capture of an everyday scene.', '2009-12-01 16:16:32.000000', NULL, 1),
