(5748893, 836691, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives:The overall scene holds together very well and I think the Lensbaby is the right tool for the job. I''m really liking the grain too. Also, I wonder how you got this shot - the timing is either highly fortuitous or you camped out - either way it makes for a great scene.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: There is a lot of blur here and I wonder if a smaller aperture ring might have been a little more effective - but then perhaps that would detract from the overall vision.<br/> <br/>Overall: A most compelling image - it gets better and better the longer I look at it.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives:The overall scene holds together very well and I think the Lensbaby is the right tool for the job. I''m really liking the grain too. Also, I wonder how you got this shot - the timing is either highly fortuitous or you camped out - either way it makes for a great scene. Critical stuff: There is a lot of blur here and I wonder if a smaller aperture ring might have been a little more effective - but then perhaps that would detract from the overall vision. Overall: A most compelling image - it gets better and better the longer I look at it.', '2009-12-01 17:02:31.000000', NULL, 1),
