(5750906, 836751, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives: Very mysterious (that comment was typed by my 8 year old while I was making tea and I couldn''t have put it better myself). Though I will add ''Wow!'' look at the distant reflection - fantastic. The lighting here is sensational - as shot or augmented with something like Viveza or Sliver Efex Pro using control points? I''m a fan of the deep piano shadow too.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing at all.<br/> <br/>Overall: Artistically and technically, a very impressive image.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-12-08 05:29:06.</i></td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives: Very mysterious (that comment was typed by my 8 year old while I was making tea and I couldn''t have put it better myself). Though I will add ''Wow!'' look at the distant reflection - fantastic. The lighting here is sensational - as shot or augmented with something like Viveza or Sliver Efex Pro using control points? I''m a fan of the deep piano shadow too. Critical stuff: Nothing at all. Overall: Artistically and technically, a very impressive image.', '2009-12-02 16:45:39.000000', '2009-12-08 05:29:06.000000', 1),
(5750909, 836753, 109309, '<td valign="top">I love this. Urban exploration type photos are one of my favorite types of photos, Not sure if its because of the way nature takes over once we have left a place or seeing these historical or not so historical buildings (albeit in a dilapidated condition) It''s amazing how a place "dies" once its abandoned</td>', 'I love this. Urban exploration type photos are one of my favorite types of photos, Not sure if its because of the way nature takes over once we have left a place or seeing these historical or not so historical buildings (albeit in a dilapidated condition) It''s amazing how a place "dies" once its abandoned', '2009-12-02 16:47:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(5750911, 834603, 109309, '<td valign="top">Amazing capture</td>', 'Amazing capture', '2009-12-02 16:47:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(5750930, 836706, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives: Great perspective, composition and story. I think you''re very brave to offer this up in the FS for the voters - a vote splitter for sure. However, I think there is much to reward the patient viewer - the guy in the doorway, the bottle in the hand of the other guy - nothing contrived here; it offers a raw feel.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Just the above really, the image is what it is and it will appeal to a minority.<br/> <br/>Overall: Good, gritty work.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives: Great perspective, composition and story. I think you''re very brave to offer this up in the FS for the voters - a vote splitter for sure. However, I think there is much to reward the patient viewer - the guy in the doorway, the bottle in the hand of the other guy - nothing contrived here; it offers a raw feel. Critical stuff: Just the above really, the image is what it is and it will appeal to a minority. Overall: Good, gritty work.', '2009-12-02 16:55:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(5750939, 836760, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives: Very interesting abstract image - suggests a neon forest (if there was such a thing). The density of the trails is just right and I really like the colour variance from top to bottom.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Some of the highlights towards the bottom are a little blown and if I''m honest I think this does detract from your otherwise excellent execution.<br/> <br/>Overall: A very attractive vibrant image.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives: Very interesting abstract image - suggests a neon forest (if there was such a thing). The density of the trails is just right and I really like the colour variance from top to bottom. Critical stuff: Some of the highlights towards the bottom are a little blown and if I''m honest I think this does detract from your otherwise excellent execution. Overall: A very attractive vibrant image.', '2009-12-02 16:59:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(5750950, 835711, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives: A very effective image done with journalistic intent - serves to remind us what we have. The POV makes the image; I''m trying to work out from where you shot this. It does work very well.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: The toning of the monochrome treatment is excellent but I think it adds a level of abstraction which might detract from some of the image''s power. The slight skewing of reality allows us the luxury to see a photo rather than life - I imagine this monochrome version is a better photo but I''m not sure it is better journalism.<br/> <br/>Overall: Great choice for FS - I thank you for bringing us the real world.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives: A very effective image done with journalistic intent - serves to remind us what we have. The POV makes the image; I''m trying to work out from where you shot this. It does work very well. Critical stuff: The toning of the monochrome treatment is excellent but I think it adds a level of abstraction which might detract from some of the image''s power. The slight skewing of reality allows us the luxury to see a photo rather than life - I imagine this monochrome version is a better photo but I''m not sure it is better journalism. Overall: Great choice for FS - I thank you for bringing us the real world.', '2009-12-02 17:05:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(5750959, 836833, 38930, '<td valign="top">Nice angle!  I would just say to lose the border, and lower the white balance to make this look a lot "cooler."  With that cool, bluish look, this image work much nicer.  Great idea though!</td>', 'Nice angle!  I would just say to lose the border, and lower the white balance to make this look a lot "cooler."  With that cool, bluish look, this image work much nicer.  Great idea though!', '2009-12-02 17:09:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(5750961, 836266, 38930, '<td valign="top">Great fog!  What an awesome location... nice work!</td>', 'Great fog!  What an awesome location... nice work!', '2009-12-02 17:09:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(5750965, 836007, 38930, '<td valign="top">Wow, this is amazing!  Nice shot!</td>', 'Wow, this is amazing!  Nice shot!', '2009-12-02 17:10:02.000000', NULL, 1),
