(5752382, 833480, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives:This one jumps right out at you, the contrast between the red machines and the blue sky makes the image for me. The POV accentuates the size of these beasts too.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Although I like the tone mapping. I think I''d have tried to do something to suppress some of the haloing. Also, some of the highlights in the clouds are blown which is a little distracting.<br/> <br/>Overall: Quite a powerful image, certainly one worth offering up in a FS.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives:This one jumps right out at you, the contrast between the red machines and the blue sky makes the image for me. The POV accentuates the size of these beasts too. Critical stuff: Although I like the tone mapping. I think I''d have tried to do something to suppress some of the haloing. Also, some of the highlights in the clouds are blown which is a little distracting. Overall: Quite a powerful image, certainly one worth offering up in a FS.', '2009-12-03 13:51:13.000000', NULL, 1),
