(5752468, 836879, 79838, '<td valign="top">Amazing place, very nice shot.<br/>Would love to visit this place some time.<br/>Where is it ??</td>', 'Amazing place, very nice shot.Would love to visit this place some time.Where is it ??', '2009-12-03 14:26:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752474, 834691, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives: This is a very nice minimalistic landscape. If I was going to guess on the photographer I would say: <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=58691" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">signal2noise</a>. I love this coloration, it works so well with the mist and the off-centeredness of the tree is perfect.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing at all.<br/> <br/>Overall: Very nice minimalistic image.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives: This is a very nice minimalistic landscape. If I was going to guess on the photographer I would say:  signal2noise. I love this coloration, it works so well with the mist and the off-centeredness of the tree is perfect. Critical stuff: Nothing at all. Overall: Very nice minimalistic image.', '2009-12-03 14:34:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752479, 832056, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives: Wow, I love this - has a slight <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=72103" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">dougi555</a> feel about it but I''m really not sure - I''d expect to see higher contrast across the whole frame if it were, but then the emphasis on the sphere would be lost. I really like the way the image is about so many things - the building, the figure, the sphere, the water - all there, all contributing but none dominating to the exclusion of the other elements.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: I still wonder about how it would look with a crisper, more contrasty background / building-scape....<br/> <br/>Overall: A very fine image of a most interesting scene.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives: Wow, I love this - has a slight  dougi555 feel about it but I''m really not sure - I''d expect to see higher contrast across the whole frame if it were, but then the emphasis on the sphere would be lost. I really like the way the image is about so many things - the building, the figure, the sphere, the water - all there, all contributing but none dominating to the exclusion of the other elements. Critical stuff: I still wonder about how it would look with a crisper, more contrasty background / building-scape.... Overall: A very fine image of a most interesting scene.', '2009-12-03 14:43:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752484, 836605, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives: Great use of motion blur here and the monochrome treatment is an excellent choice. I even like the bold border. It would be tempting to reject this image due to the primary subject being this unsharp but I''m glad you''ve had the confidence to ignore such restrictive conventions.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing at all.<br/> <br/>Overall: Great stuff.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives: Great use of motion blur here and the monochrome treatment is an excellent choice. I even like the bold border. It would be tempting to reject this image due to the primary subject being this unsharp but I''m glad you''ve had the confidence to ignore such restrictive conventions. Critical stuff: Nothing at all. Overall: Great stuff.', '2009-12-03 14:45:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752486, 833789, 100393, '<td valign="top">Wonderful focus and this works so well in monochrome.</td>', 'Wonderful focus and this works so well in monochrome.', '2009-12-03 14:46:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752491, 836718, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives: There is a great sense of texture to the wall and the glass and the just-enough light works really well with the coloration. The composition for your subject is pretty sympathetic too.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: I think the intrinsic interest level in this scene is very low and although I like what you have done with, I don''t really feel that it adds up to something that can inspire as some other images too.<br/> <br/>Overall: This is certainly a competent piece of work, but it isn''t one that is pushing my buttons.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives: There is a great sense of texture to the wall and the glass and the just-enough light works really well with the coloration. The composition for your subject is pretty sympathetic too. Critical stuff: I think the intrinsic interest level in this scene is very low and although I like what you have done with, I don''t really feel that it adds up to something that can inspire as some other images too. Overall: This is certainly a competent piece of work, but it isn''t one that is pushing my buttons.', '2009-12-03 15:01:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752499, 833034, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives: As soon as I looked at this I thought <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=36606" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">AlexSaberi</a>, a swan, a deep black backdrop and fabulous execution. I''m not at all convinced that I''m right but that photographer popped into my head straight away. This really is an excellent image though - so much more than the sum of its parts. I LOVE the way this buck convention and shows us the wrong end of an animal.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing at all.<br/> <br/>Overall: Superb work.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives: As soon as I looked at this I thought  AlexSaberi, a swan, a deep black backdrop and fabulous execution. I''m not at all convinced that I''m right but that photographer popped into my head straight away. This really is an excellent image though - so much more than the sum of its parts. I LOVE the way this buck convention and shows us the wrong end of an animal. Critical stuff: Nothing at all. Overall: Superb work.', '2009-12-03 15:05:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752540, 834504, 103142, '<td valign="top">I really like the  idea of this. I''m curious what it would have looked like at a little lower point of view. Fun shot. 7</td>', 'I really like the  idea of this. I''m curious what it would have looked like at a little lower point of view. Fun shot. 7', '2009-12-03 15:32:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752543, 834114, 103142, '<td valign="top">I love this! Very nicely done!</td>', 'I love this! Very nicely done!', '2009-12-03 15:32:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752545, 832288, 103142, '<td valign="top">ooh!! I want to go there!! 9</td>', 'ooh!! I want to go there!! 9', '2009-12-03 15:33:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752546, 836878, 103142, '<td valign="top">Seems a tad washed out. I wouldn''t want to over saturate it, but I think the subtle colors have flattened it a bit too much. Perhaps it just needs a bit more contrast if you want the softer look? 6</td>', 'Seems a tad washed out. I wouldn''t want to over saturate it, but I think the subtle colors have flattened it a bit too much. Perhaps it just needs a bit more contrast if you want the softer look? 6', '2009-12-03 15:34:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752603, 834132, 56828, '<td valign="top">I would have rated this higher if the dark of I''m assuming the arms framing her, didn''t distract me.  Especially in the left corner...It took me a long time to figure out what that was....but when I say I would have rated it higher I mean I would have given more than the 8 that I just gave it.</td>', 'I would have rated this higher if the dark of I''m assuming the arms framing her, didn''t distract me.  Especially in the left corner...It took me a long time to figure out what that was....but when I say I would have rated it higher I mean I would have given more than the 8 that I just gave it.', '2009-12-03 16:05:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752637, 836753, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives:Great perspective here and a really interesting locale to shoot in. The graffiti offers some welcome colour too. The shadow and light on the floor is pretty compelling too.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: A minor niggle but the slight clipping of the final graffiti letter does bother me a little. I think there is only so much interest to be had in this scene - I do think you have made the most of what is here but I''m not sure that is enough to make a standout image.<br/> <br/>Overall: A very competent image of a dramatic room.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives:Great perspective here and a really interesting locale to shoot in. The graffiti offers some welcome colour too. The shadow and light on the floor is pretty compelling too. Critical stuff: A minor niggle but the slight clipping of the final graffiti letter does bother me a little. I think there is only so much interest to be had in this scene - I do think you have made the most of what is here but I''m not sure that is enough to make a standout image. Overall: A very competent image of a dramatic room.', '2009-12-03 16:46:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752647, 836800, 18197, '<td valign="top">A stark reminder of the power of the sea. I like it, especially for its composition, color saturation and subject matter. Crop is a little tighter than I might have done.</td>', 'A stark reminder of the power of the sea. I like it, especially for its composition, color saturation and subject matter. Crop is a little tighter than I might have done.', '2009-12-03 16:52:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752649, 836307, 18197, '<td valign="top">Interesting photo with an interesting perspective. Keeping the flag in the frame was a good choice.</td>', 'Interesting photo with an interesting perspective. Keeping the flag in the frame was a good choice.', '2009-12-03 16:52:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752650, 831694, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives: Well, I''ll try to offer something here - I do like the colour of the sky and the skeletal silhouettes of the trees are well demonstrated.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: I''m sorry but I think there just isn''t enough going on here to hold a viewers interest; I was going to say that the image is too small (and it is) but in this case I don''t think it really matters, because I don''t think there is too much we are missing at any size.<br/> <br/>Overall: I''m genuinely puzzled, you must''ve seen something in this image to offer it up; I only wish I could see it too.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-12-08 06:51:35.</i></td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives: Well, I''ll try to offer something here - I do like the colour of the sky and the skeletal silhouettes of the trees are well demonstrated. Critical stuff: I''m sorry but I think there just isn''t enough going on here to hold a viewers interest; I was going to say that the image is too small (and it is) but in this case I don''t think it really matters, because I don''t think there is too much we are missing at any size. Overall: I''m genuinely puzzled, you must''ve seen something in this image to offer it up; I only wish I could see it too.', '2009-12-03 16:52:54.000000', '2009-12-08 06:51:35.000000', 1),
(5752652, 836814, 18197, '<td valign="top">Made me smile. Didn''t know an animal could pick its own nose with its own tongue.</td>', 'Made me smile. Didn''t know an animal could pick its own nose with its own tongue.', '2009-12-03 16:53:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752653, 836264, 100393, '<td valign="top">Very well executed image. Love the grain.</td>', 'Very well executed image. Love the grain.', '2009-12-03 16:53:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752654, 836563, 18197, '<td valign="top">This has an historic feel to it which is appropriate to the subject. Well done!</td>', 'This has an historic feel to it which is appropriate to the subject. Well done!', '2009-12-03 16:54:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752656, 836792, 18197, '<td valign="top">I like the photo especially because of its great lighting and ceiling detail. Good work.</td>', 'I like the photo especially because of its great lighting and ceiling detail. Good work.', '2009-12-03 16:55:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752659, 836795, 18197, '<td valign="top">I really like this. Partly because of the colors and high contrast. Partly because of the unusual crop and the subject matter. Not normally a letterbox border fan, but it well supports this image so I even like that.</td>', 'I really like this. Partly because of the colors and high contrast. Partly because of the unusual crop and the subject matter. Not normally a letterbox border fan, but it well supports this image so I even like that.', '2009-12-03 16:56:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752660, 836661, 100393, '<td valign="top">Goodness me! I didn''t see it to begin with! Funny and bold!</td>', 'Goodness me! I didn''t see it to begin with! Funny and bold!', '2009-12-03 16:58:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752661, 836908, 18197, '<td valign="top">What a terrific and dynamic photo! Because the boom is hidden by the smoke, it looks like the bucket is suspended on the stream of water. Then you realize it''s an illusion. Cool. Well composed, captured, presented. Among the best of the challenge.</td>', 'What a terrific and dynamic photo! Because the boom is hidden by the smoke, it looks like the bucket is suspended on the stream of water. Then you realize it''s an illusion. Cool. Well composed, captured, presented. Among the best of the challenge.', '2009-12-03 16:58:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752662, 836695, 100393, '<td valign="top">Impressive capture.</td>', 'Impressive capture.', '2009-12-03 16:58:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752666, 836811, 100393, '<td valign="top">This is the 3rd fluffy pony shot I''ve come across - this is the most interesting!</td>', 'This is the 3rd fluffy pony shot I''ve come across - this is the most interesting!', '2009-12-03 17:00:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752667, 836719, 100393, '<td valign="top">This is a very interesting landscape shot - great stuff.</td>', 'This is a very interesting landscape shot - great stuff.', '2009-12-03 17:01:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752676, 836669, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives:I feel that you''ve captured a sense of wildness here - it''s almost chaotic; I suspect you''ve captured the feel of what it would be like to be there. I like the coloration too.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: The image does seem a little out of alignment, I get the sense that it should be rotated slightly counterclockwise - I can see how this contribute to the choas I like but it still bugs me a little.<br/> <br/>Overall: A very effective image - one that has the capacity to transport the viewer.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives:I feel that you''ve captured a sense of wildness here - it''s almost chaotic; I suspect you''ve captured the feel of what it would be like to be there. I like the coloration too. Critical stuff: The image does seem a little out of alignment, I get the sense that it should be rotated slightly counterclockwise - I can see how this contribute to the choas I like but it still bugs me a little. Overall: A very effective image - one that has the capacity to transport the viewer.', '2009-12-03 17:08:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752706, 836778, 18197, '<td valign="top">This has an artistic feeling and I could see it in a gallery or as a backdrop to a magazine piece.</td>', 'This has an artistic feeling and I could see it in a gallery or as a backdrop to a magazine piece.', '2009-12-03 17:29:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752708, 836688, 18197, '<td valign="top">Wow, what a cool lizard. Love the vibrant colors and the wonderful detail.</td>', 'Wow, what a cool lizard. Love the vibrant colors and the wonderful detail.', '2009-12-03 17:30:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752711, 836314, 18197, '<td valign="top">Feels like where I grew up. Thanks for the nostalgia trip. Your photo makes me want to go hiking there.</td>', 'Feels like where I grew up. Thanks for the nostalgia trip. Your photo makes me want to go hiking there.', '2009-12-03 17:32:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752717, 836749, 23484, '<td valign="top">Nice POV. Great job on the detail.</td>', 'Nice POV. Great job on the detail.', '2009-12-03 17:34:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752720, 836741, 23484, '<td valign="top">That ridge of light is cool. Beautiful image.</td>', 'That ridge of light is cool. Beautiful image.', '2009-12-03 17:35:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752722, 836691, 23484, '<td valign="top">Neat shot. Love the focus.</td>', 'Neat shot. Love the focus.', '2009-12-03 17:36:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752724, 836616, 23484, '<td valign="top">Nice job on the detail.  The colors all seem to blend.</td>', 'Nice job on the detail.  The colors all seem to blend.', '2009-12-03 17:37:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752725, 836658, 23484, '<td valign="top">Great shot. I love the framing.</td>', 'Great shot. I love the framing.', '2009-12-03 17:37:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752728, 836761, 23484, '<td valign="top">I don''t know how everything doesn''t get flooded. Nice perspective.</td>', 'I don''t know how everything doesn''t get flooded. Nice perspective.', '2009-12-03 17:38:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752729, 834983, 23484, '<td valign="top">Nice job on the lighting.</td>', 'Nice job on the lighting.', '2009-12-03 17:38:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752731, 836778, 23484, '<td valign="top">I really like the softness.  Nice job on the processing.</td>', 'I really like the softness.  Nice job on the processing.', '2009-12-03 17:39:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752733, 833628, 23484, '<td valign="top">Very nice job capturing all three styles.</td>', 'Very nice job capturing all three styles.', '2009-12-03 17:40:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752738, 836907, 23484, '<td valign="top">Nice perspective.  The lighting was perfect for this shot.</td>', 'Nice perspective.  The lighting was perfect for this shot.', '2009-12-03 17:41:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752740, 836593, 23484, '<td valign="top">Cool idea for a wall to jump.</td>', 'Cool idea for a wall to jump.', '2009-12-03 17:42:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752744, 833187, 23484, '<td valign="top">Very nice image. I love the layers</td>', 'Very nice image. I love the layers', '2009-12-03 17:43:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752745, 836698, 23484, '<td valign="top">Absolutely perfect job on the city lights. How many shots did it take to get them this good?</td>', 'Absolutely perfect job on the city lights. How many shots did it take to get them this good?', '2009-12-03 17:44:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752747, 836812, 23484, '<td valign="top">Nice colors. Great job on the processing.</td>', 'Nice colors. Great job on the processing.', '2009-12-03 17:44:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752748, 836600, 23484, '<td valign="top">Very interesting job on the processing. Nice job.</td>', 'Very interesting job on the processing. Nice job.', '2009-12-03 17:45:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752770, 836708, 27770, '<td valign="top">Nice capture..so hard to get in focus while coming at you...great work!</td>', 'Nice capture..so hard to get in focus while coming at you...great work!', '2009-12-03 18:03:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752841, 836808, 18197, '<td valign="top">Beautifully saturated. Dramatically composed.</td>', 'Beautifully saturated. Dramatically composed.', '2009-12-03 19:28:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752843, 836663, 18197, '<td valign="top">Made me smile. Love the expression, the setting, the B&amp;W treatments, the dof, ... pretty much everything.</td>', 'Made me smile. Love the expression, the setting, the B&W treatments, the dof, ... pretty much everything.', '2009-12-03 19:29:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752845, 836651, 18197, '<td valign="top">I like that you caught some stars and i like the overall feeling of this.</td>', 'I like that you caught some stars and i like the overall feeling of this.', '2009-12-03 19:29:49.000000', NULL, 1);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(5752847, 836718, 18197, '<td valign="top">This demonstrates your mastery of camera and post processing. It''s well composed. But for me the subject isn''t that interesting.</td>', 'This demonstrates your mastery of camera and post processing. It''s well composed. But for me the subject isn''t that interesting.', '2009-12-03 19:30:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752848, 836832, 18197, '<td valign="top">Pigeons are tough to photograph. They''re quick and twitchy. Good job with focus, detail, color, composition.</td>', 'Pigeons are tough to photograph. They''re quick and twitchy. Good job with focus, detail, color, composition.', '2009-12-03 19:32:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752849, 836397, 18197, '<td valign="top">Well composed and captured candid moment. Nicely processed to take advantage of shallow DOF.</td>', 'Well composed and captured candid moment. Nicely processed to take advantage of shallow DOF.', '2009-12-03 19:32:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752851, 836905, 18197, '<td valign="top">You''ve done a nice job capturing the flowing lines of the clouds and the tree line. Maybe a little dark, but that''s personal taste.</td>', 'You''ve done a nice job capturing the flowing lines of the clouds and the tree line. Maybe a little dark, but that''s personal taste.', '2009-12-03 19:35:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752853, 836724, 18197, '<td valign="top">This is a bold photo ... bold lines, bold contrast. Certainly draws you into the scene.</td>', 'This is a bold photo ... bold lines, bold contrast. Certainly draws you into the scene.', '2009-12-03 19:36:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752854, 836899, 18197, '<td valign="top">Nice capture of the flowing water. Great focus on the static elements (e.g. leaves). Pretty place.</td>', 'Nice capture of the flowing water. Great focus on the static elements (e.g. leaves). Pretty place.', '2009-12-03 19:37:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752856, 836922, 18197, '<td valign="top">This grabbed my attention. The contrast between crisp watch features and sand (?) is striking. Makes me want to grab the watch and brush it clean. Strong photographic contrast sets it off very well. I''m not a fan of letter box framing and in this case, I think it diminished the photo a little.</td>', 'This grabbed my attention. The contrast between crisp watch features and sand (?) is striking. Makes me want to grab the watch and brush it clean. Strong photographic contrast sets it off very well. I''m not a fan of letter box framing and in this case, I think it diminished the photo a little.', '2009-12-03 19:39:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752858, 836669, 18197, '<td valign="top">I''m glad I''m not in this scene. I dislike winter and you''ve captured what i dislike about it perfectly.</td>', 'I''m glad I''m not in this scene. I dislike winter and you''ve captured what i dislike about it perfectly.', '2009-12-03 19:40:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752861, 836818, 18197, '<td valign="top">Terrific detail you''ve captured in the squirrel. Superb DOF. Well lit. I like it.</td>', 'Terrific detail you''ve captured in the squirrel. Superb DOF. Well lit. I like it.', '2009-12-03 19:41:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752862, 836486, 18197, '<td valign="top">Survival of the fittest. Well seen, captured and presented. Like the border.</td>', 'Survival of the fittest. Well seen, captured and presented. Like the border.', '2009-12-03 19:42:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752863, 836861, 18197, '<td valign="top">Love the faces, their expressions, the costumes and their colors. It looks like they are having fun. Border is a little gimmicky ... makes me wonder what was there you''re trying to hide. Not a huge factor, more of a nit.</td>', 'Love the faces, their expressions, the costumes and their colors. It looks like they are having fun. Border is a little gimmicky ... makes me wonder what was there you''re trying to hide. Not a huge factor, more of a nit.', '2009-12-03 19:43:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752866, 836605, 18197, '<td valign="top">I like the energy you''ve captured here. B&amp;W was a good choice. But your border unsells the motion. If you must use the letter box ... a wider aspect ratio would sell the motion better. I''m not a letterbox fan ... so ignore my ramblings on framing as the ravings of an ignorant.</td>', 'I like the energy you''ve captured here. B&W was a good choice. But your border unsells the motion. If you must use the letter box ... a wider aspect ratio would sell the motion better. I''m not a letterbox fan ... so ignore my ramblings on framing as the ravings of an ignorant.', '2009-12-03 19:45:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(5752868, 836878, 18197, '<td valign="top">Nice view of Toronto''s skyline. I like Toronto and it has some neat architecture. I like the reflections you''ve captured here. Photo feels a bit over exposed. Maybe a bit more contrast would offset that, make it pop a bit more.</td>', 'Nice view of Toronto''s skyline. I like Toronto and it has some neat architecture. I like the reflections you''ve captured here. Photo feels a bit over exposed. Maybe a bit more contrast would offset that, make it pop a bit more.', '2009-12-03 19:47:54.000000', NULL, 1),
