(5754148, 831077, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives: I always like to see Lensbaby images in the FS. I like the way the light illuminates the steps and the sense of movement you have captured.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: If I''m honest, I''m not sure there''s enough intrinsic interest in the scene for it to be a compelling image.<br/> <br/>Overall: Quite nicely done but it isn''t an image that appeals to me.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives: I always like to see Lensbaby images in the FS. I like the way the light illuminates the steps and the sense of movement you have captured. Critical stuff: If I''m honest, I''m not sure there''s enough intrinsic interest in the scene for it to be a compelling image. Overall: Quite nicely done but it isn''t an image that appeals to me.', '2009-12-04 11:28:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(5754149, 836254, 35086, '<td valign="top">Rustic feel, neutral tones and food is always so pleasing, that''s almost cheating! ;)</td>', 'Rustic feel, neutral tones and food is always so pleasing, that''s almost cheating! ;)', '2009-12-04 11:28:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(5754152, 836254, 100393, '<td valign="top">Lovely tones and lighting here.</td>', 'Lovely tones and lighting here.', '2009-12-04 11:29:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(5754158, 835829, 100393, '<td valign="top">That''s a lot of birds - pretty good shot too! The saturation of the skin tones is a little high but I like the rest of it.</td>', 'That''s a lot of birds - pretty good shot too! The saturation of the skin tones is a little high but I like the rest of it.', '2009-12-04 11:30:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(5754160, 836776, 35086, '<td valign="top">The back light makes for an interesting silhouettes. The colors and contrasts are so harsh, seems almost over saturated.</td>', 'The back light makes for an interesting silhouettes. The colors and contrasts are so harsh, seems almost over saturated.', '2009-12-04 11:31:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(5754161, 835034, 100393, '<td valign="top">Very nicely executed image.</td>', 'Very nicely executed image.', '2009-12-04 11:31:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(5754167, 836235, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives: This image is all about light and shadow and you''ve set up and captured the balance between the two perfectly. The colour and texture is really good too.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: I have mixed feelings about the border - right colour choice but I can''t help thinking that the pear perhaps doesn''t need its help. I wonder if you''d have framed it if the DPC background was black.<br/> <br/>Overall: A very accomplished piece of work.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives: This image is all about light and shadow and you''ve set up and captured the balance between the two perfectly. The colour and texture is really good too. Critical stuff: I have mixed feelings about the border - right colour choice but I can''t help thinking that the pear perhaps doesn''t need its help. I wonder if you''d have framed it if the DPC background was black. Overall: A very accomplished piece of work.', '2009-12-04 11:34:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(5754173, 833597, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives: I''m afraid I''m really going to struggle to put something here.... I suppose I do like the way that you have managed to capture / emphasise the joints between the piece of turf.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: I''m afraid I don''t really get this image, there''s little intrinsic interest and your PP does little to add to a quite boring scene.<br/> <br/>Overall: Apologies, I''m sure you see something of interest here but it is beyond me.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives: I''m afraid I''m really going to struggle to put something here.... I suppose I do like the way that you have managed to capture / emphasise the joints between the piece of turf. Critical stuff: I''m afraid I don''t really get this image, there''s little intrinsic interest and your PP does little to add to a quite boring scene. Overall: Apologies, I''m sure you see something of interest here but it is beyond me.', '2009-12-04 11:39:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(5754181, 836896, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives: Very delicately done - the whole look is very much in keeping with the subject. The very narrow zone of focus is highly interesting, but for me the highlight is the shadow!<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing really<br/> <br/>Overall: A very precise piece of work which gets the most out of a simple subject.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-12-08 05:38:46.</i></td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives: Very delicately done - the whole look is very much in keeping with the subject. The very narrow zone of focus is highly interesting, but for me the highlight is the shadow! Critical stuff: Nothing really Overall: A very precise piece of work which gets the most out of a simple subject.', '2009-12-04 11:41:43.000000', '2009-12-08 05:38:46.000000', 1),
(5754182, 836905, 100393, '<td valign="top">Crazy crop. I''m afraid there isn''t a lot that is working for me with this image.</td>', 'Crazy crop. I''m afraid there isn''t a lot that is working for me with this image.', '2009-12-04 11:42:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(5754183, 836465, 100393, '<td valign="top">Beautifully done.</td>', 'Beautifully done.', '2009-12-04 11:42:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(5754185, 836741, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives: Wow, the quality of the light here stopped me in my tracks - the coloration too is sublime. The whole scene is quite magical and looks very much like a miniature.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing at all<br/> <br/>Overall: Very interesting image.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-12-08 05:48:25.</i></td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives: Wow, the quality of the light here stopped me in my tracks - the coloration too is sublime. The whole scene is quite magical and looks very much like a miniature. Critical stuff: Nothing at all Overall: Very interesting image.', '2009-12-04 11:44:48.000000', '2009-12-08 05:48:25.000000', 1),
(5754193, 835977, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives: Great candid image, excellent colours and bags of interest - makes me wonder what I would see to the left and right of your image.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: I do wish the focus on the face was a little crisper and that the black thing at the top of the frame was either not there or made more sense.<br/> <br/>Overall: An interesting shot which I have been pleased to have found.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives: Great candid image, excellent colours and bags of interest - makes me wonder what I would see to the left and right of your image. Critical stuff: I do wish the focus on the face was a little crisper and that the black thing at the top of the frame was either not there or made more sense. Overall: An interesting shot which I have been pleased to have found.', '2009-12-04 11:48:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(5754198, 836802, 35086, '<td valign="top">This almost looks like a painting!  I guess that''s always good. :)</td>', 'This almost looks like a painting!  I guess that''s always good. :)', '2009-12-04 11:51:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(5754200, 836167, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives: Nice motion blur image, there are lots of elements to look at and they are all so different, the couple of runners, the bus itself (and its route information), the passengers and (most of all for me), the poster on the side. This is one of those images that reminds us that there is always so much to look at around us if only we were to lift our gaze.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Perhaps a tighter crop top to bottom, allowing the bus to fill the height of the frame.<br/> <br/>Overall: The ordinary made interesting. Good job.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives: Nice motion blur image, there are lots of elements to look at and they are all so different, the couple of runners, the bus itself (and its route information), the passengers and (most of all for me), the poster on the side. This is one of those images that reminds us that there is always so much to look at around us if only we were to lift our gaze. Critical stuff: Perhaps a tighter crop top to bottom, allowing the bus to fill the height of the frame. Overall: The ordinary made interesting. Good job.', '2009-12-04 11:52:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(5754201, 834616, 35086, '<td valign="top">Although I like night photography, this piece seems to lack a lot of elements which usually makes these kinds of shot interesting.  Very sorry, it doesn''t stimulate me at all. :(</td>', 'Although I like night photography, this piece seems to lack a lot of elements which usually makes these kinds of shot interesting.  Very sorry, it doesn''t stimulate me at all. :(', '2009-12-04 11:53:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(5754206, 836841, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives: This is a very pretty image - I''m really glad that you''ve had the confidence to trust in its blurry goodness. The slight coloration works really well too.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: I can''t think of anything.<br/> <br/>Overall: I glad you trusted your instincts here - good convention bucking stuff.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives: This is a very pretty image - I''m really glad that you''ve had the confidence to trust in its blurry goodness. The slight coloration works really well too. Critical stuff: I can''t think of anything. Overall: I glad you trusted your instincts here - good convention bucking stuff.', '2009-12-04 11:55:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(5754207, 836757, 35086, '<td valign="top">You captured some very nice colors with this one.  But some elements are throwing me off such as the centered horizon, the edge of the road and the harsh bright spots in the sky.  Still a pleasing sight to see, though.  Very dreamy. :)</td>', 'You captured some very nice colors with this one.  But some elements are throwing me off such as the centered horizon, the edge of the road and the harsh bright spots in the sky.  Still a pleasing sight to see, though.  Very dreamy. :)', '2009-12-04 11:55:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(5754209, 833034, 35086, '<td valign="top">Nice details on the feathers and of course, brilliant contrast!  I get where you were going with the composition and motion but it somehow feels a little, what''s the word, ''confined''?  Still very nice. :)</td>', 'Nice details on the feathers and of course, brilliant contrast!  I get where you were going with the composition and motion but it somehow feels a little, what''s the word, ''confined''?  Still very nice. :)', '2009-12-04 11:58:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(5754210, 834824, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives: Shot through some form of fabric I presume; it works just like an overlay - I really like it. The success of the image lies in its ability to conceal and reveal to just the right amount. Lighting and colour are sublime.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing at all.<br/> <br/>Overall: Excellent work.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives: Shot through some form of fabric I presume; it works just like an overlay - I really like it. The success of the image lies in its ability to conceal and reveal to just the right amount. Lighting and colour are sublime. Critical stuff: Nothing at all. Overall: Excellent work.', '2009-12-04 11:58:08.000000', NULL, 1),
